      "content": "Sneaky risks in a warehouse setting are often related to the infrastructure itself, which is where the true danger hides. A common oversight is the integrity of secondary containment or drainage systems, which might be subtly compromised, allowing small solvent leaks to pool unnoticed beneath the racking or in floor drains. Another \"behind-the-scenes\" issue is the degradation of electrical equipment—old wiring, improperly rated junction boxes, or faulty sensors—which can provide the ignition source without any visible evidence of misuse. These failures are insidious because they don't look like a direct violation of storage protocol; they look like normal wear and tear.",
